    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "15. Stratagems",
    "ruleNumber": "15.11",
    "summary": "When the opponent finishes their Charge phase, pick one friendly, unengaged unit at most 12″ from an enemy unit. A VEHICLE must also have CHARACTER or WALKER. Choose a mode when paying CP, before the roll, and resolve the charge using Charge Step. Leap to Defend costs 1 CP before modifiers. Choose only enemies in reach that already completed a charge move during this phase. Into the Fray starts at 2 CP. After charge roll modifiers, reduce results above 6 to 6. You may choose any enemy unit that meets two tests: at most 6″ away, and no farther than the roll allows. Apply CP modifiers to the chosen mode’s full starting price.",
